WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.472
What you should have by Friday.

2
00:00:01.752 --> 00:00:16.984
By the end of week 1: a one-page scope doc, a risk register ranked by exposure with the top three mitigated or in progress, an eval set of at least 100 tagged cases with a sealed held-out split, a baseline run logged against it,

3
00:00:17.264 --> 00:00:22.064
and a repo whose CI runs on every commit even though there is barely any code.

4
00:00:22.344 --> 00:00:32.733
That last item matters more than it looks: when every later change runs through CI from the start, quality checks become routine rather than a cleanup job in week 5.

5
00:00:33.013 --> 00:00:38.005
Next week you build retrieval, and you will measure it against this baseline from the first run.
